tamework.ui.guide.topic.travelFlight.note=These are separate systems. Use the companion's mode controls for companion flight and the flight HUD for avatar abilities.
tamework.ui.guide.topic.worldUtilities.title=World utilities
tamework.ui.guide.topic.worldUtilities.body=SCARECROW PLACEMENT\nPlace a Tamework scarecrow on a solid surface. It faces the placer. Look at it and hold its collection prompt for one second to pick it up; if inventory is full, it stays placed.\n\nCOVERAGE\nAutomatic NPC spawn markers are paused within 32 blocks. Ordinary spawning is suppressed in native spawn chunks intersecting that area, so its horizontal edge can extend to a chunk boundary. Overlapping scarecrows remain active independently until collected.\n\nWHAT STILL EXISTS OR SPAWNS\nScarecrows do not remove existing creatures. Manually triggered spawn markers, spawner items, commands, breeding, recall, and other deliberate scripted spawns can still create or move animals.\n\nTROUGHS AND COOPS\nSupported troughs provide care resources and need refilling. Supported coops store and release animals. Their prompts and the companion's card explain the current state.\n\nSee Care & happiness for feeding and water, and Capture & coops for storage. Availability of these utilities depends on the installed content.
tamework.ui.guide.topic.worldUtilities.visual=Protected area ≠ empty area
tamework.ui.guide.topic.worldUtilities.note=The scarecrow limits automatic spawning. Animals already inside and deliberate arrivals such as breeding or recall remain possible.
